      "title": "Preferred provider organizations",
      "narration": "A PPO is a network of hospitals and physicians that have agreed to provide care to plan members at discounted fees. Members may see any provider, but the plan pays a higher share in network and a lower share out of network, and in-network providers accept the allowance as payment in full. There is no gatekeeper; members see specialists without referrals. PPOs are fee-for-service arrangements: the provider is paid per service at the negotiated rate. Marcus’s employer offers a PPO because it preserves choice while the network discounts hold down premiums.",
