      "title": "Open and closed panels",
      "narration": "Panel describes who may join the network and whom the providers may treat. An open panel PPO or IPA-model HMO contracts with independent providers who also treat patients from other plans, and it admits any qualified provider willing to accept its terms. A closed panel, typical of staff and group model HMOs, uses providers who serve only that plan’s members. For members, open panels mean more choice and a better chance their current doctor participates. For plans, closed panels mean tighter control over practice patterns. Exclusive provider organizations, or EPOs, use a PPO-style network but cover nothing out of network except emergencies.",
