      "title": "Point-of-service plans",
      "narration": "A point-of-service plan is an HMO with an escape hatch. Inside the network the member uses a primary care physician, obtains referrals and pays copayments, exactly as in an HMO. At the point of service, when care is needed, the member may instead go outside the network, and the plan pays indemnity-style benefits with a deductible and coinsurance, usually leaving the member with higher costs. The POS design answers the biggest objection to HMOs, loss of choice, while keeping the gatekeeper for most care. Members should understand that out-of-network use often requires them to file their own claims.",
