      "narration": "Priya asks Theo which design her bakery should offer. He frames the trade-off. An HMO costs least and restricts most. A PPO costs more and lets members see specialists anywhere, with incentives to stay in network. A POS sits between, with a gatekeeper in network and coverage out. An EPO looks like a PPO but pays nothing out of network. The right answer depends on the workforce: employees with established specialists value PPO freedom; younger employees may prefer the HMO premium. Whatever the design, Maryland’s mandated benefits and the federal essential health benefit rules apply.",
