      "title": "TRICARE",
      "narration": "TRICARE is the Department of Defense health program for active duty service members, retirees, National Guard and Reserve members and their families. Its options mirror civilian designs. TRICARE Prime works like an HMO, with a primary care manager, referrals and low out-of-pocket costs, and is mandatory for active duty members. TRICARE Select works like a PPO, allowing self-referral to network providers with cost sharing. TRICARE For Life supplements Medicare for retirees 65 and older, paying after Medicare. A private health policy generally excludes care TRICARE furnishes, which is the government plan exclusion you saw in Lesson 9.",
