      "title": "Preferred providers and balance billing",
      "text": "A preferred provider contractually accepts the plan’s negotiated fee as payment in full, so an in-network member owes only the deductible, coinsurance or copayment. An out-of-network provider has no such contract and may bill the difference between its charge and the plan’s allowance, subject to federal surprise-billing protections for emergencies and certain facility-based care.",
